Original commit body from f4cc104:

Single source of truth for route metadata: all route information is now
exclusively stored in meta.concepts[].{path, method} instead of being
duplicated to legacy fields (route_path, http_method).

Changes:
- Removed dual-population code from framework_patterns.py (lines 775-785, 809-816)
- Updated http.py linker to only read from concepts (removed legacy fallback)
- Updated openapi.py linker with concept-based route detection
- Added _has_route_concept() and _get_route_info_from_concept() helpers
- Updated all tests to verify concepts instead of legacy fields

This completes the migration to the concept-based metadata system,
eliminating potential data inconsistencies between legacy fields and
concepts that could mask bugs or cause incorrect behavior.
